# config/escalation-alert - active alert channels for real away-mode
# escalations (bin/fm-supervise-daemon.sh's escalation_alert_notify). Copy this
# into a local, gitignored config/escalation-alert and edit. Same directive
# syntax as config/wedge-alarm, but this fires on every SUCCESSFUL delivery of
# a genuine escalation digest (a PR ready for review, an ask-user decision, a
# real blocker) rather than only when injection itself wedges - so an away
# captain can be pinged the moment something actually needs them.
#
# Directives:
#   off              disable this alert entirely (the pane digest still delivers)
#   auto | default   platform default: macOS -> osascript; other platforms have
#                    no built-in OS channel (configure a command: line instead)
#   osascript        macOS Notification Center banner (backend-independent)
#   herdr            herdr UI notification (herdr notification show)
#   command:<cmd>    run <cmd> via `sh -c`; the escalation summary is passed as
#                    $1 and on stdin, so it can reach a phone/pager while away
#
# An ABSENT config/escalation-alert behaves as `off`: this is a new
# captain-facing notification capability, so it is opt-in, unlike
# config/wedge-alarm's default-on `auto`.
# Unlike config/wedge-alarm, there is no extra rate limit beyond the natural
# escalation-batch window: each flushed digest already batches every wake that
# arrived within that window, so a distinct later escalation still pings.
#
# Example: a macOS banner plus a push to a phone via ntfy.sh, so a real
# escalation reaches you even away from the machine.
osascript
command: curl -fsS -H "Title: firstmate escalation" -d "$1" https://ntfy.sh/replace-with-your-topic
